  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q19-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "There are 22 black sheep and 28 white sheep in a paddock.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q19-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What fraction of the sheep are black?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{11}{25}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Fraction black}&=\\frac{22}{22+28}\\\\\\text{Fraction black}&=\\frac{22}{50}\\\\\\text{Fraction black}&=\\frac{11}{25}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q19-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many black sheep must be added to the paddock so that $\\frac{8}{15}$ of the sheep are black?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p7-q19-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "10 black sheep.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p7-q19-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Let ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " be the number added and solve ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{22+x}{50+x}=\\frac{8}{15}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Let $x$ be the number of black sheep added. There are then $22+x$ black sheep out of $50+x$ sheep.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{22+x}{50+x}&=\\frac{8}{15}\\\\15(22+x)&=8(50+x)\\\\330+15x&=400+8x\\\\15x-8x&=400-330\\\\7x&=70\\\\x&=10\\end{align*}$$\n\nAdd 10 black sheep. The resulting fraction is $\\frac{32}{60}=\\frac{8}{15}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      }
    ]
  },
